    "explanation": "To both parties: this is the dispute over the SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-02754 after the driver terminated it at 14:23:41 on 16 Sep 2026 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW.\n\nThe driver did reach the pickup point. EV-TRIP-02754 records the driver's 'arrived' event at 14:22:40, and EV-GPS-02754 places his fixes inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, closest approach about 1.1 m, with 7 qualifying in-geofence fixes. POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) therefore hold, and the arrival marker is not false: at the marker the driver was stationary (0 kph) and about 1.1 m from the pin, so neither the 'more than 300 m' nor the '15 kph or above' trigger of POL-NS-05 is met and no false-arrival referral is recorded against him.\n\nThe fee nevertheless fails on the waiting limb. POL-NS-01(c) requires the driver to hold position inside the geofence for a continuous dwell of at least the free waiting period in force for this trip - 180 seconds, read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec - measured from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix and not from the 'arrived' tap. EV-GPS-02754 shows a single continuous in-geofence run of 57 seconds, from 14:22:40 to 14:23:37: a shortfall of 123 seconds. The platform's own wait timer agrees, running only from 14:22:42 to the 14:23:41 cancellation, about 59 seconds. Limb (c) fails. Under POL-NS-06 a dwell shorter than the free waiting period makes the cancellation fee not chargeable and refunds it in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she responded to messages. The accumulation route in POL-NS-06(i) is not open: the trace shows one in-geofence interval only (run_count 1), and the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02754-01 is MISSING (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0, no payload), so there is no second interval to sum and no advisory to assert.\n\nThe sum in issue is the cancellation-fee line of SGD 4.50 in EV-FARE-02754, which reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of SGD 4.50; payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.00. The full SGD 4.50 therefore returns to the rider, and no driver compensation is payable, POL-NS-06 providing that none is due on a shortfall and POL-NS-01 providing that a failed limb yields no compensation.\n\nThe driver's claims are accepted so far as they go - the arrival, the honest marker and the clean fare line are all correct - but they do not answer limb (c), which is the limb the charge breaks on. On the rider's POL-NS-04 point ('coming out now', 14:23:40): the fee is already disposed of under POL-NS-06, so that clause need not be run, and the outcome is unchanged either way. On the profile point raised by the driver's counterstatement: POL-GEN-01 makes prior_no_show_flags context only and it can never ground a finding; the trailing counter the policy does name, rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d, stands at 1, below the 3 that POL-NS-09(d) requires, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming test is not met (1 no-show termination against 58 completed trips in 30 days), so no escalation is owed on either profile. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: every artifact carrying the deciding fact is clean at weight_multiplier 1.0, so there is no POL-NS-08(a)-(d) impairment and no POL-NS-09(e), and confidence is not capped below the 0.70 floor. POL-NS-12 does not apply because the arrival marker on this trip is BUTTON, not GPS_AUTO.\n\nNo clause produces a referral on these facts, so the referrals list is empty. The monetary effect of SGD 4.50 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the refund executes on issue. My confidence of 0.95 is capped by the weight of the artifacts that carry the deciding dwell fact, EV-GPS-02754 and EV-TRIP-02754, both at 1.0."
